#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:1
msgid "llvm-extract - extract a function from an LLVM module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:8
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-extract` \\[*options*\\] **--func** *function-name* "
"\\[*filename*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:12
msgid ""
"The {program}`llvm-extract` command takes the name of a function and "
"extracts it from the specified LLVM bitcode file. It is primarily used as a "
"debugging tool to reduce test cases from larger programs that are triggering "
"a bug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:16
msgid ""
"In addition to extracting the bitcode of the specified function, {program}"
"`llvm-extract` will also remove unreachable global variables, prototypes, "
"and unused types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:20
msgid ""
"The {program}`llvm-extract` command reads its input from standard input if "
"filename is omitted or if filename is `-`. The output is always written to "
"standard output, unless the **-o** option is specified (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:24
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:27
msgid ""
"Extract the alias named *function-name* from the LLVM bitcode. May be "
"specified multiple times to extract multiple alias at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:32
msgid ""
"Extract the alias matching *alias-regular-expr* from the LLVM bitcode. All "
"alias matching the regular expression will be extracted. May be specified "
"multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:38
msgid ""
"Extract basic blocks(s) specified in *basic-block-specifier*. May be "
"specified multiple times. Each \\<function:bb[;bb]> specifier pair will "
"create a function. If multiple basic blocks are specified in one pair, the "
"first block in the sequence should dominate the rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:45
msgid "Delete specified Globals from Module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:49
msgid ""
"Enable binary output on terminals. Normally, {program}`llvm-extract` will "
"refuse to write raw bitcode output if the output stream is a terminal. With "
"this option, {program}`llvm-extract` will write raw bitcode regardless of "
"the output device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:56
msgid ""
"Extract the function named *function-name* from the LLVM bitcode. May be "
"specified multiple times to extract multiple functions at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:61
msgid ""
"Extract the function(s) matching *function-regular-expr* from the LLVM "
"bitcode. All functions matching the regular expression will be extracted. "
"May be specified multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:67
msgid ""
"Extract the global variable named *global-name* from the LLVM bitcode. May "
"be specified multiple times to extract multiple global variables at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:72
msgid ""
"Extract the global variable(s) matching *global-regular-expr* from the LLVM "
"bitcode. All global variables matching the regular expression will be "
"extracted. May be specified multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:78
msgid "Preserve the values of constant globals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:82
msgid "Recursively extract all called functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:86
msgid "Print a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:90
msgid ""
"Specify the output filename. If filename is \"-\" (the default), then "
"{program}`llvm-extract` sends its output to standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:95
msgid "Write output in LLVM intermediate language (instead of bitcode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:98
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-extract.md:100
msgid ""
"If {program}`llvm-extract` succeeds, it will exit with 0. Otherwise, if an "
"error occurs, it will exit with a non-zero value."
msgstr ""

